# serve.transcript -- the production tool's answers, pinned: one request a line, its answer the next.
#
# Kit_serve answers these today (ocaml/engine/kit/kit_serve.ml), and test_transcript.ml replays
# every one through `serve_line` (`eff serve`), byte for byte. It is the net under the kit's move
# onto generated names (seat GEN, phase 1) and under the lowered transition of slice 1.7: an answer
# that moves fails the test at its line. `eff mcp` serves the authoring tool (Kit_mcp,
# test_mcp.ml), not these commands.
#
#   serve> REQUEST  a request line, through serve_line
#   < ANSWER        the answer to the line above
#
# Never edit an answer by hand. A deliberate change of answer is one reviewed diff:
#   cd ocaml && E4_KIT_TRANSCRIPT_REWRITE=$PWD/engine/test/kit/serve.transcript \
#     opam exec --switch=effect4 -- dune test --force engine/test/kit

## check: the type, and a refusal of each kind (typing, admission)
